# The execution pair (FABLE-OPUS-CODE-DATA-SPLIT-20260925-189 commit 2; next_core_tasks.md §3 item 7):
# every activation of `keep` runs over a fresh instance of its data prototype in the unit's slot
# answering it, and the slot shows the latest one.
# - keep(1) reaches `int: v 7`, and the slot then shows its instance: keep\v is 7 (h).
# - keep(0) returns before the declaration, so its fresh instance keeps the prototype's 0 -- not the
#   7 of the activation before.
# h * 10 + keep\v is 70.  A shared occurrence (until -189) gives 77; an activation that writes an
# instance other than the one its slot shows gives 0.
fn: keep (int: go) int
    if: go = 0
        return: 0
    int: v 7
    return: 0
end: keep

fn: probe () int
    int: h 0
    int: g 0
    keep(1)
    h: keep\v
    keep(0)
    g: h * 10 + keep\v
    return: g
end: probe

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: probe(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
